{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Until an anointed prince, seven weeks</b> — Now these are nineteen years, which are the reigns of Cyrus and Ahasuerus and two years of Darius, and he reigned twelve years, and thus it is written in the Book of the Kings of Persia, and twenty years of King Artaxerxes." "<b>And now, seven weeks</b> — until Nehemiah came, as written in the book of Ezra, and sixty-two weeks during which the Second House stood, and half the week I have explained. And he said: 'desolate' — and it is a passive participle. And the meaning is that it is desolate to all who see it and all who hear of it from Israel." "(27) <b>And the meaning of 'until the end, decreed, is poured out upon the desolate'</b> — that the abomination will stand in the House until the time of the end arrives and is decreed. 'Decreed, poured out upon the desolate' — this is the abomination, by way of prayer: that it be desolate, like: 'Daughter Babylon, the devastated one.'"], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra reads the phrase תתך על שומם as referring to the abomination itself, understood as a prayer that it remain desolate; the comparison is to Isaiah 47:1, השדודה, which I render 'the devastated one' to match his reading of שומם as a passive state."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:44.596732512Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}